{"chunk_id": "5abc5ccf7814", "text": "With the monkey search party despairing of ever crossing the ocean to find Sita, the aged Jambavan addresses Hanuman, who sits quietly apart. He reminds the army that their success depends on the one hero capable of the task and calls Hanuman forth. To awaken Hanuman\u2019s forgotten power, Jambavan recounts his divine origin: born to Anjana through the wind\u2011god Vayu, blessed with immense strength, intelligence, and speed. As a child, Hanuman once leapt skyward to seize the rising sun as if it were a fruit, was struck by Indra\u2019s thunderbolt, and afterward received boons of invulnerability and near\u2011immortality from the gods. Jambavan concludes by urging him to rise and cross the ocean like Vishnu striding the worlds, transforming the monkeys\u2019 despair into hope and setting the stage for Hanuman\u2019s legendary leap to Lanka.\nJambavan encourages Hanuman to recall his divine origin and immense powers, urging him to leap the ocean and save the despairing monkey army.\nThemes: awakening hidden power, divine birth of Hanuman, leadership and encouragement, destiny and duty", "vector": [-0.0010208027670159936, -0.034387726336717606, 0.0019306667381897569, 0.01773696579039097, -0.010424938052892685, 0.017061397433280945, -0.01235891692340374, -0.022187765687704086, -0.02515496499836445, -0.006808663718402386, -0.006401335820555687, 0.02069091983139515, 0.021684400737285614, -0.008279017172753811, 0.00274035451002419, 0.0023760779295116663, 0.05007149279117584, -0.01912784017622471, 0.010722982697188854, -0.01165023259818554, -0.013398760929703712, -0.013498108834028244, -0.002477081958204508, 0.00031439567101188004, -0.012650338001549244, 0.008914845064282417, 0.025671575218439102, -0.034069810062646866, 0.017988648265600204, -0.014584315940737724, -0.0075703333131968975, -0.010835577733814716, -0.01506118755787611, -0.004536901134997606, -0.008471090346574783, 0.0032453746534883976, -0.007636565249413252, -0.0154055